1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,560
A Greek musician, a Japanese
god and seven Cherokee men

2
00:00:04,560 --> 00:00:08,460
all went into the land of the
dead to bring someone back.

3
00:00:08,580 --> 00:00:12,160
Each was given a rule —
and each of them broke it.

4
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:14,260
Start with the one you know.

5
00:00:14,280 --> 00:00:20,120
Orpheus, whose lyre could move even
stones, lost his wife Eurydice to a snake.

6
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:22,260
In the underworld, he played for the king

7
00:00:22,260 --> 00:00:25,120
and queen of the dead,
and they were moved.

8
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:28,120
She could follow him back,
they said, on one condition:

9
00:00:28,120 --> 00:00:32,580
he must not look back until they
had both reached the upper world.

10
00:00:32,680 --> 00:00:35,320
Within sight of the daylight, he turned.

11
00:00:35,760 --> 00:00:37,680
She was taken back.

12
00:00:38,040 --> 00:00:43,680
The Japanese tell it about a god, in the
Kojiki, a book finished in the year 712.

13
00:00:43,940 --> 00:00:47,300
Izanami had died giving
birth, and her husband,

14
00:00:47,360 --> 00:00:50,100
Izanagi, followed her
to the land of the dead.

15
00:00:50,180 --> 00:00:53,400
The world they had made was
not finished, he told her.

16
00:00:53,400 --> 00:00:54,400
Come back.

17
00:00:54,560 --> 00:00:56,480
It was too late, she said.

18
00:00:56,500 --> 00:00:59,240
She had already eaten
the food of that land.

19
00:00:59,280 --> 00:01:01,100
But she would ask its gods.

20
00:01:01,360 --> 00:01:04,520
"Look not at me," she
said, and went inside.

21
00:01:04,660 --> 00:01:05,660
He waited.

22
00:01:05,960 --> 00:01:11,820
At last Izanagi broke a tooth from his
comb, lit it like a torch, and went in.

23
00:01:11,960 --> 00:01:16,500
Maggots swarmed over her body, and
eight gods of thunder lived in it.

24
00:01:16,500 --> 00:01:17,500
He ran.

25
00:01:17,580 --> 00:01:21,660
"You have shamed me," she said,
and sent the dead after him.

26
00:01:21,700 --> 00:01:24,960
He threw down his headdress,
and it turned into grapes.

27
00:01:25,040 --> 00:01:28,380
He threw down his comb, and
it became bamboo shoots.

28
00:01:28,460 --> 00:01:32,500
At the foot of the pass, three peaches
put the rest of them to flight.

29
00:01:32,600 --> 00:01:34,920
Then Izanami came herself.

30
00:01:35,140 --> 00:01:37,580
Izanagi blocked the pass
with a boulder that would

31
00:01:37,580 --> 00:01:41,140
take a thousand men to lift,
and across it they spoke.

32
00:01:41,240 --> 00:01:46,100
If he did this, she said, every day she
would strangle a thousand of his people.

33
00:01:46,100 --> 00:01:51,580
Then every day, he answered, he would
build fifteen hundred birth huts.

34
00:01:51,680 --> 00:01:55,340
So, in this story, people die every day.

35
00:01:55,340 --> 00:01:58,240
And every day, children are born.

36
00:01:58,660 --> 00:02:02,860
On another continent, the Cherokee
tell it about the daughter of the Sun.

37
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:07,780
James Mooney published it in 1900
under the heading "Origin of death."

38
00:02:07,840 --> 00:02:10,640
The Sun's heat killed
the people with fever.

39
00:02:10,640 --> 00:02:14,280
They tried to kill her, and a
rattlesnake bit her daughter instead.

40
00:02:14,280 --> 00:02:17,820
The Sun wept, and the world went dark.

41
00:02:17,880 --> 00:02:21,040
The people were told to bring
her back from the Ghost country.

42
00:02:21,180 --> 00:02:23,640
Seven men went, carrying a box.

43
00:02:23,760 --> 00:02:25,640
They found the dead dancing,

44
00:02:25,640 --> 00:02:29,860
struck the Sun's daughter down as
she passed, and shut her in the box.

45
00:02:29,980 --> 00:02:35,200
Their one rule: do not open it, not
even a little way, until you are home.

46
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:36,960
On the road she woke.

47
00:02:37,080 --> 00:02:38,420
She asked for food.

48
00:02:38,420 --> 00:02:39,300
For water.

49
00:02:39,300 --> 00:02:40,060
For air.

50
00:02:40,060 --> 00:02:43,580
They were afraid she was dying,
and they lifted the lid a little.

51
00:02:43,580 --> 00:02:46,420
Something fluttered out into the thicket.

52
00:02:46,520 --> 00:02:47,600
A redbird.

53
00:02:48,020 --> 00:02:51,260
When they reached the
settlements, the box was empty.

54
00:02:51,560 --> 00:02:55,540
Three stories, three
rules: do not look at her,

55
00:02:55,540 --> 00:02:58,940
do not look back, do not open the box.

56
00:02:59,280 --> 00:03:02,060
None of the three was
broken out of carelessness.

57
00:03:02,500 --> 00:03:04,440
Izanagi could not wait.

58
00:03:04,640 --> 00:03:07,360
Orpheus could not bear not to see her.

59
00:03:07,400 --> 00:03:10,320
The Cherokee men were
afraid she was dying.

60
00:03:10,760 --> 00:03:14,880
Folklorists have recorded this tale
among many Native American peoples.

61
00:03:15,340 --> 00:03:16,340
Why?

62
00:03:16,500 --> 00:03:17,760
Nobody knows.

63
00:03:18,040 --> 00:03:22,340
A few think it is very old, carried
to America by the first people who

64
00:03:22,340 --> 00:03:26,980
crossed from Asia, though others
doubt any myth can be traced so far.

65
00:03:27,120 --> 00:03:30,280
One Swedish scholar argued
that such tales grew from

66
00:03:30,280 --> 00:03:33,060
the journeys of shamans
into the land of the dead.

67
00:03:33,060 --> 00:03:36,660
And some think no one
had to pass it on at all.

68
00:03:36,860 --> 00:03:39,140
Every people has lost someone.

69
00:03:39,440 --> 00:03:42,940
Every people has asked
why they do not come back.

70
00:03:43,220 --> 00:03:45,960
The Cherokee tale ends
with its own answer.

71
00:03:46,100 --> 00:03:48,340
If the men had kept the box closed,

72
00:03:48,340 --> 00:03:51,300
we could bring back our
friends from the Ghost country.

73
00:03:51,400 --> 00:03:55,340
But now, when they die, we
can never bring them back.

74
00:03:55,620 --> 00:04:00,560
Three peoples, three rules, and
one mistake anyone would make.

75
00:04:00,560 --> 00:04:04,640
If you like stories that turn
up again in places far apart,

76
00:04:04,640 --> 00:04:07,620
leave a like and subscribe
to Animated Tales.

77
00:04:07,700 --> 00:04:08,842
Until next time.
